  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat, singleprofile) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a clear +4.2% improvement over rna_only baseline (config_001: 0.485/0.464), establishing that the multimodal concat pipeline is the current best direction. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) meaningfully affects performance, and this is a critical design choice that will propagate to all future multimodal experiments. What this tests: config_017 is identical to config_016 except fusion=weighted, giving a clean single-variable A/B comparison of fusion strategies with the same encoders and profile setting. Why it is the best next step: with only two experiments completed, we should first lock down the best fusion strategy within the already-promising multimodal + pca_n2000 + resnet50 region before branching to other axes (multiprofile, alternative encoders). The result will be unambiguous—either weighted improves on concat (a direct gain) or concat is confirmed as the better choice—reducing uncertainty about a decision that affects every subsequent multimodal configuration. This is a low-risk, high-information exploitation step that maximizes the value of the next experiment under a tight budget."
}

